@startuml
title Finance Management Platform - GUI Delivery Context

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 12
}

actor "Personal User" as PersonalUser
actor "Household Member" as HouseholdUser <<planned>>
actor "Company Finance User" as BusinessUser <<planned>>

rectangle "Graphical Desktop Environment\nTkinter + Matplotlib" as Desktop <<external platform>>
rectangle "Finance Management Platform\n\nTransaction management\nStatistics and visualization\nShared financial state" as FinanceSystem <<system>>
database "Shared SQLite Database\n\ndata/finance_tracker.db" as Ledger <<external storage>>

PersonalUser --> FinanceSystem : Packaged GUI: add, query, and delete transactions;\nundo/redo; view statistics and dashboard
FinanceSystem --> PersonalUser : Transaction lists, summaries, charts,\nand operation results
HouseholdUser ..> FinanceSystem : Future household GUI <<planned>>
BusinessUser ..> FinanceSystem : Future company-finance GUI <<planned>>

FinanceSystem --> Desktop : Render windows and charts
Desktop --> FinanceSystem : Mouse, keyboard, and window events

FinanceSystem --> Ledger : Atomically save transactions, budgets,\nand application metadata
Ledger --> FinanceSystem : Load the shared financial state\nand storage revision

note bottom of FinanceSystem
  The packaged product exposes a graphical interface only.
  Personal finance is implemented in the current release.
  Household and company-finance interfaces are planned extensions.
end note

note bottom of Ledger
  The packaged GUI uses the SQLite database beside the executable.
  SQLite is embedded and does not require a database server.
  The current system has no cloud synchronization, remote API,
  or third-party payment platform.
end note

@enduml
